          "question": "type 1 here, been sick all day, meter says 24 and the ketone strip went dark purple, my breath smells odd",
          "answer": "**Get emergency care now. Call your local emergency number or go to the nearest emergency department. Do not wait and see.** A dark purple ketone reading, feeling unwell and an unusual breath smell in someone with type 1 diabetes can be signs of diabetic ketoacidosis. The reference guidance says diabetic emergencies of this kind \"develop over hours to days and are life-threatening\" (Diabetic emergencies: very high and very low blood sugar, red-flag guidance). Ask someone to come with you, and do not drive yourself if you feel unwell.\n\nThe automated urgency check returned \"routine\" because no rule in its table matched your wording. I am not relying on that result. Your description fits the warning pattern in the guidance, so please act on the advice above.\n\n**Your glucose reading:** The meter number of 24 could be mmol/L or mg/dL, and the two mean very different things. Check which unit your meter uses. Either way, a normal-looking glucose does not rule out ketoacidosis. The guidance notes that ketoacidosis can occur at near-normal glucose levels.\n\n**Get help immediately, or call emergency services, if you have any of these:**\n- Vomiting that won't stop, or you cannot keep fluids down\n- Deep, fast or laboured breathing\n- Severe or worsening belly pain\n- Drowsiness, confusion, or being hard to wake\n- Fainting or feeling faint when standing\n- A meter reading \"HI\" or a glucose value you cannot make sense of\n- Any sense that you are getting worse\n\nIllness raises insulin needs, and insulin should not simply be stopped when you are unwell. Your diabetes team should have agreed sick-day guidance with you in advance (red-flag guidance, same source). Tell the emergency team that you are type 1 and have high ketones.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
